E
"3 stumps"
"Low to the ground each stump shows signs of the axe work that was done to fell
the tree.  Some of the stumps are small, the trees cleared simply to make
room.  Some are larger and perhaps were used in the building of something.
"
-1
S

#11001
"Woodland Path"
"Trees still form an effective perimeter to the path here but obvious signs of
labored work to clear them is evident.  Ragged stumps dot a newly forged wide
forest trail that shows many deep tracks heading in all directions as if
whoever made them carried heavy loads, perhaps the trees they felled.  To the
east a hastily constructed shack of poor craftsmanship sits nestled amid the
trees.
"
""
